Level 1 is a massive, concrete warehouse or parking garage characterized by pillars, hanging fluorescent lights, and a consistent supply of electricity.

Unbranded red, blue, white, or black cars occasionally appear in the garage of Level 1, though they are always non-functional and lack license plates.

The alloy found in the cars within Level 1 is a valuable mixture of carbon, iron, platinum, and titanium used to craft armor and weapons.

Puddles of Almond Water on the concrete floors of Level 1 frequently evaporate into a thick, low-hanging fog that never fully clears.

Periodic power outages in Level 1 can plunge the entire area into total darkness for days at a time, allowing hostile entities to hunt.

Rusted pieces of rebar and jagged metal often jut out from the concrete walls of Level 1, posing a significant infection risk to wanderers.

Certain electrical sockets found in Level 1 have been measured at an output of up to one gigawatt despite having no identifiable power source.

These white-walled corridors are accessible through jet-black metallic doors in Level 1 and often contain toolboxes, plywood, and tables.

These are exceptionally clean, bright sections of Level 1 that span for miles and are popular locations for groups to establish permanent bases.

These stationary entities in Level 1 disguise themselves as harmless pools of Almond Water but are actually deep pits lined with sharp teeth.

Skin-Stealers, These pale humanoids found in Level 1 can wear the skin of victims to blend in and often mimic human voices to lure wanderers.

Drawings and portraits found on the warehouse walls of Level 1 are sentient entities capable of tracking a wanderer’s movements with their eyes.

Predatory paintings in Level 1 can reach out from their frames to grab wanderers, pulling them into the artwork as unresponsive drawings.

Wooden crates containing canned food or Almond Water appear and disappear at irregular intervals throughout the various halls of Level 1.

Deceptive supply crates in Level 1 sometimes contain Liquid Pain, a foul-smelling black substance that causes extreme internal damage if touched.

a major M.E.G. outpost in Level 1 houses 60 members who trade supplies and provide guidance to lost wanderers.

